.TH 7ZFM-QT 1 "November 2026" "7zfm-qt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
7zfm-qt \- Qt port of the 7-Zip File Manager and of 7zG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 7zfm-qt
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B 7zfm-qt
.I command
.RI [ switches ...]
.RI [ archive ]
.RI [ files ...]
.br
.B 7zfm-qt
.B \-\-extract\fR|\fB\-\-extract\-here\fR|\fB\-\-extract\-to\fR|\fB\-\-test
.IR archives ...
.br
.B 7zfm-qt
.B \-\-add\fR|\fB\-\-add\-7z\fR|\fB\-\-add\-zip\fR|\fB\-\-hash\-file
.IR files ...
.br
.B 7zfm-qt
.B \-\-hash
.I method
.IR files ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 7zfm-qt
is a port of the Windows 7-Zip File Manager (7zFM) to Qt 6, built on
upstream 7-Zip as a library. It opens archives, disk images, partitions and
file systems by their signature rather than their extension, and opens
nested ones in place, without extracting them first.
.PP
With no arguments, or with a
.IR path ,
it opens the file manager there: a folder, or an archive or image to browse.
Without a path, each panel reopens the folder it showed last.
.PP
With a 7-Zip
.I command
as the first argument, it works as upstream's
.BR 7zG :
it takes the command line of
.BR 7z (1),
runs the command with 7-Zip's dialogs and progress window instead of console
output, and exits. The file manager window is not shown. A file whose name is
one of the command letters is opened with a path, as in
.BR "7zfm-qt ./x" .
.SH COMMANDS
These are the commands of
.BR 7zG ;
letters are accepted in either case.
.TP
.B a
Add files to an archive, creating it if needed.
.TP
.B u
Update files in an archive.
.TP
.B d
Delete files from an archive.
.TP
.B e
Extract files without their paths, into one folder.
.TP
.B x
Extract files with their full paths.
.TP
.B t
Test the integrity of archives.
.TP
.B h
Calculate checksums of files (CRC32 by default; see
.BR \-scrc ).
.TP
.B b
Run the benchmark.
.SH SWITCHES
Every switch of
.BR 7z (1)
is accepted and means the same. The most used ones:
.TP
.B \-ad
Show the dialog first: the Extract dialog for
.B e
and
.BR x ,
the Add to Archive dialog for
.BR a .
This switch exists only in
.BR 7zG .
.TP
.BI \-o dir
Extract into
.IR dir .
A
.B *
in
.I dir
is replaced with the archive's name without its extension, so
.B \-o*
extracts each archive into a folder of its own name.
.TP
.B \-spe
Eliminate the duplicate root folder: when the archive holds a single folder
with the output folder's name, extract its contents directly.
.TP
.BI \-t type
Archive type, such as
.BR 7z ,
.BR zip ,
.B tar
or
.BR iso .
.TP
.BI \-m ...
Compression method and its parameters, such as
.B \-mx=9
or
.BR \-m0=lzma2 .
.TP
.BI \-p password
Use
.IR password .
Without
.IR password ,
it is asked for in a dialog.
.TP
.B \-r
Recurse into subfolders.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-x
Include or exclude files by name or wildcard, as in
.BR 7z (1).
.TP
.B \-an \-ai!\fIarchive\fR ...
Take the archive names from
.B \-ai
switches instead of the first file argument, so that one
.B x
or
.B t
command handles several archives.
.TP
.BI \-scrc method
Checksum method for
.BR h :
.BR CRC32 ,
.BR CRC64 ,
.BR XXH64 ,
.BR MD5 ,
.BR SHA1 ,
.BR SHA256 ,
.BR SHA384 ,
.BR SHA512 ,
.BR SHA3\-256 ,
.BR BLAKE2sp ,
or
.B *
for all of them.
.TP
.BI \-v size
Create volumes of
.IR size ,
such as
.BR \-v100m .
.TP
.B \-y
Assume Yes on all questions, such as replacing files.
.SH MENU COMMANDS
The context-menu entries that the packages install for
.BR dolphin (1),
.BR nemo (1),
.BR pcmanfm\-qt (1),
.BR caja (1)
(with caja-actions) and
.BR thunar (1)
(with thunar-archive-plugin) run these instead of a 7-Zip command line. They
work out folder and archive names from the selection, as the Explorer menu of
7-Zip on Windows does, which a static menu file cannot express in
.BR 7z (1)
syntax. Each file is a separate argument.
.TP
.B \-\-extract
Extract files...: the Extract dialog, set to a folder named after the
archive, or to
.B */
for several archives.
.TP
.B \-\-extract\-here
Extract Here: into the archive's folder.
.TP
.B \-\-extract\-to
Extract to "\fIname\fR/": into a folder named after the archive, next to it,
eliminating the duplicate root folder as
.B \-spe
does.
.TP
.B \-\-test
Test archive.
.TP
.B \-\-add
Add to archive...: the Add to Archive dialog, with the archive named after
the file, or after its folder for several files.
.TP
.BR \-\-add\-7z ", " \-\-add\-zip
Add to "\fIname\fR.7z" or "\fIname\fR.zip", without a dialog.
.TP
.BI \-\-hash " method"
CRC SHA: show the checksums of the files and folders, with
.I method
as for
.BR \-scrc .
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-file
CRC SHA > SHA-256 -> \fIname\fR.sha256: write a SHA-256 checksum file next
to the files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For a 7-Zip command, as
.BR 7z (1):
.TP
.B 0
No error.
.TP
.B 1
Warning: some files could not be processed.
.TP
.B 2
Fatal error.
.TP
.B 7
Command line error.
.TP
.B 8
Not enough memory.
.TP
.B 255
Stopped by the user.
.PP
A menu command exits with 2 when it is given no files or a file that does
not exist, with 1 when adding fails, and otherwise with 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/7zfm-qt/7zfm-qt.conf
Settings: the options of the Tools menu, the folders the panels show and the
compression dialog's history, as 7-Zip keeps them in the Windows registry.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B 7zfm-qt disk.vhdx
Open a disk image in the file manager.
.TP
.B 7zfm-qt x backup.7z \-o/tmp/restore
Extract an archive with a progress window.
.TP
.B 7zfm-qt x \-ad \-an \(aq\-ai!*.zip\(aq \(aq\-o*\(aq
Choose the options in the Extract dialog, then extract every zip file in the
current folder into a folder of its own name.
.TP
.B 7zfm-qt a \-ad docs.7z ~/Documents
Open the Add to Archive dialog for a folder.
.TP
.B 7zfm-qt h \-scrcSHA256 image.iso
Show the SHA-256 of a file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 7z (1),
.BR 7zz (1)
.PP
https://github.com/ringosham/7zfm-qt
